IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa8-regulative.l4: the principal duties, prohibitions and permissions of Companies Act 2006 ss 362 to 414B, as regulative rules over the
-- keel's `Party`, each with a typed action under its own section label. LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- The same duties are also encoded as decision functions in the other coa8 modules; those are the tested form (check.sh counts their assertions).
-- A #TRACE prints no assertion line, so check.sh cannot see a wrong outcome here: the outcomes below are written as comments from the text
-- and were compared by eye with what both binaries print (NOTES.md, "What the stable binary does not accept").
-- Clock: the unit of every number is a day, and a trace starts at day 0, the day the duty arises.

§§ `Prohibitions and duties as regulative rules`

-- ---- s 366(1): authorisation required --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 366(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 366(1) make a political donation or incur political expenditure without the authorisation this Part requires`

-- src:4695 | (1) A company must not—
-- src:4696 | (a) make a political donation to a political party or other political organisation, or to an independent election candidate, or
-- src:4697 | (b) incur any political expenditure,
-- src:4698 | unless the donation or expenditure is authorised in accordance with the following provisions.
@ref s 366(1) Authorisation required for donations or expenditure (src:4695-4698)
`s 366(1) the company shall not make an unauthorised donation or incur unauthorised expenditure` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    SHANT `s 366(1) make a political donation or incur political expenditure without the authorisation this Part requires`
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company made a political donation or incurred political expenditure that this Part did not authorise (section 366(1))"

-- the company does it on day 3: the prohibition is broken. Expected: BREACH BY Company.
#TRACE `s 366(1) the company shall not make an unauthorised donation or incur unauthorised expenditure` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 366(1) make a political donation or incur political expenditure without the authorisation this Part requires` AT 3
-- the company does nothing: the prohibition stands, unbroken. Expected: the prohibition printed back as the residual.
#TRACE `s 366(1) the company shall not make an unauthorised donation or incur unauthorised expenditure` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- ---- s 369(2): the directors in default make good --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 369(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 369(2)(a) make good to the company the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure, with interest`
    `s 369(2)(b) compensate the company for any loss or damage resulting from the unauthorised donation or expenditure`

-- src:4740 | (2) The directors in default are jointly and severally liable—
-- src:4741 | (a) to make good to the company the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure, with interest, and
-- src:4742 | (b) to compensate the company for any loss or damage sustained by it as a result of the unauthorised donation or expenditure having been made.
@ref s 369(2) Joint and several liability of the directors in default (src:4740-4742)
`s 369(2) the director in default shall make good and compensate` MEANS
    (PARTY Director
     MUST `s 369(2)(a) make good to the company the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure, with interest`
     LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "the director in default did not make good to the company the unauthorised amount with interest (section 369(2)(a))")
    RAND
    (PARTY Director
     MUST `s 369(2)(b) compensate the company for any loss or damage resulting from the unauthorised donation or expenditure`
     LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "the director in default did not compensate the company for its loss or damage (section 369(2)(b))")

-- the director does both: Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 369(2) the director in default shall make good and compensate` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director DOES `s 369(2)(a) make good to the company the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure, with interest` AT 10
    PARTY Director DOES `s 369(2)(b) compensate the company for any loss or damage resulting from the unauthorised donation or expenditure` AT 12
-- the director does only the first: the second remains owed. Expected: the second duty as the residual, not a breach (the text sets no time).
#TRACE `s 369(2) the director in default shall make good and compensate` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director DOES `s 369(2)(a) make good to the company the amount of the unauthorised donation or expenditure, with interest` AT 10

-- ---- s 371(1): no proceedings until 28 days after the notice ------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 371(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 371(1) bring proceedings under section 370 in the name of the company`

-- src:4772 | (1) A group of members may not bring proceedings under section 370 in the name of a company unless—
-- src:4773 | (a) the group has given written notice to the company stating—
-- src:4774 | (i) the cause of action and a summary of the facts on which the proceedings are to be based,
-- src:4775 | (ii) the names and addresses of the members comprising the group, and
-- src:4776 | (iii) the grounds on which it is alleged that those members constitute an authorised group; and
-- src:4777 | (b) not less than 28 days have elapsed between the date of the giving of the notice to the company and the bringing of the proceedings.
@ref s 371(1) The notice requirements before proceedings under section 370 (src:4772-4777)
-- The day the notice is given is day 0; the 28 days beginning with that day end on day 27, and proceedings may be brought on day 28.
`s 371(1) the group shall not bring proceedings until 28 days have passed from the notice` MEANS
    PARTY Member
    SHANT `s 371(1) bring proceedings under section 370 in the name of the company`
    WITHIN 27
    LEST BREACH BY Member BECAUSE "the group brought proceedings under section 370 less than 28 days after giving notice (section 371(1))"

-- proceedings brought on day 27, the last day of the 28: Expected: BREACH BY Member.
#TRACE `s 371(1) the group shall not bring proceedings until 28 days have passed from the notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Member DOES `s 371(1) bring proceedings under section 370 in the name of the company` AT 27
-- proceedings brought on day 28: Expected: FULFILLED (the prohibition's window has closed; nothing was done inside it).
#TRACE `s 371(1) the group shall not bring proceedings until 28 days have passed from the notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Member DOES `s 371(1) bring proceedings under section 370 in the name of the company` AT 28

-- ---- s 371(2): a director's application to the court ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 371(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 371(2) apply to the court for an order that the proposed proceedings shall not be brought`

-- src:4778 | (2) Where such a notice is given to a company, any director of the company may apply to the court within the period of 28 days beginning with the date of the giving of the notice for an order directing that the proposed proceedings shall not be brought, on one or more of the following grounds—
-- src:4779 | (a) that the unauthorised amount has been made good to the company;
-- src:4780 | (b) that proceedings to enforce the liability have been brought, and are being pursued with due diligence, by the company;
-- src:4781 | (c) that the members proposing to bring proceedings under this section do not constitute an authorised group.
@ref s 371(2) A director's application to the court (src:4778-4781)
`s 371(2) the director may apply to the court within 28 days of the notice` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MAY `s 371(2) apply to the court for an order that the proposed proceedings shall not be brought`
    WITHIN 27

-- applies on day 27: Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 371(2) the director may apply to the court within 28 days of the notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director DOES `s 371(2) apply to the court for an order that the proposed proceedings shall not be brought` AT 27
-- applies on day 28, too late. Both binaries print FULFILLED, the same as for day 27: a MAY that lapses unused is FULFILLED, so this trace cannot tell a late act from a timely one (written first as "not a performance of the permission"; finding 5). The tested form is the decision function `s 371(2) the director may apply to the court for an order that the proposed proceedings shall not be brought`.
#TRACE `s 371(2) the director may apply to the court within 28 days of the notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director DOES `s 371(2) apply to the court for an order that the proposed proceedings shall not be brought` AT 28

-- ---- s 373(1): information to the group -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 373(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 373(1) provide the group with all information relating to the subject matter of the proceedings`

-- src:4800 | (1) Where proceedings have been brought under section 370 in the name of a company by an authorised group, the group is entitled to require the company to provide it with all information relating to the subject matter of the proceedings that is in the company's possession or under its control or which is reasonably obtainable by it.
@ref s 373(1) The group's entitlement to information (src:4800)
`s 373(1) the company shall provide the group with the information` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 373(1) provide the group with all information relating to the subject matter of the proceedings`
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not provide the group with the information (section 373(1))"

-- the company provides it on day 5: Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 373(1) the company shall provide the group with the information` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 373(1) provide the group with all information relating to the subject matter of the proceedings` AT 5

-- ---- s 386(1): accounting records -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 386(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 386(1) keep adequate accounting records`

-- src:4952 | (1) Every company must keep adequate accounting records.
@ref s 386(1) Duty to keep accounting records (src:4952)
`s 386(1) the company shall keep adequate accounting records` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 386(1) keep adequate accounting records`
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not keep adequate accounting records (section 386(1))"

-- the company keeps them: Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 386(1) the company shall keep adequate accounting records` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 386(1) keep adequate accounting records` AT 1

-- ---- s 393(1): approval of accounts --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 393(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 393(1) approve accounts without being satisfied that they give a true and fair view`

-- src:5047 | (1) The directors of a company must not approve accounts for the purposes of this Chapter unless they are satisfied that they give a true and fair view of the assets, liabilities, financial position and profit or loss—
-- src:5048 | (a) in the case of the company's individual accounts, of the company;
-- src:5049 | (b) in the case of the company's group accounts, of the undertakings included in the consolidation as a whole, so far as concerns members of the company.
@ref s 393(1) The directors shall not approve accounts unless satisfied they give a true and fair view (src:5047-5049)
`s 393(1) the directors shall not approve accounts unless satisfied they give a true and fair view` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    SHANT `s 393(1) approve accounts without being satisfied that they give a true and fair view`
    LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "the director approved accounts without being satisfied that they give a true and fair view (section 393(1))"

-- a director approves accounts without being satisfied: Expected: BREACH BY Director.
#TRACE `s 393(1) the directors shall not approve accounts unless satisfied they give a true and fair view` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director DOES `s 393(1) approve accounts without being satisfied that they give a true and fair view` AT 2

-- ---- s 394 and s 414A(1): preparing the accounts and the strategic report ---------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 394 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 394 prepare individual accounts for the financial year`

-- src:5057 | The directors of every company must prepare accounts for the company for each of its financial years unless the company is exempt from that requirement under section 394A.
@ref s 394 Duty to prepare individual accounts (src:5057)
`s 394 the directors shall prepare individual accounts for the financial year` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `s 394 prepare individual accounts for the financial year`
    LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "the directors did not prepare individual accounts for the financial year (section 394)"

-- the directors prepare them: Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 394 the directors shall prepare individual accounts for the financial year` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director DOES `s 394 prepare individual accounts for the financial year` AT 100

DECLARE `s 414A(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 414A(1) prepare a strategic report for the financial year`

-- src:5401 | (1) The directors of a company must prepare a strategic report for each financial year of the company.
@ref s 414A(1) Duty to prepare a strategic report (src:5401)
`s 414A(1) the directors shall prepare a strategic report for the financial year` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `s 414A(1) prepare a strategic report for the financial year`
    LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "the directors did not prepare a strategic report for the financial year (section 414A(1))"

-- the directors prepare it: Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 414A(1) the directors shall prepare a strategic report for the financial year` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director DOES `s 414A(1) prepare a strategic report for the financial year` AT 100

-- ---- s 412(5): a director's notice to the company ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 412(5) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 412(5) give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as regulations require`

-- src:5347 | (5) It is the duty of—
-- src:5348 | (a) any director of a company, and
-- src:5349 | (b) any person who is or has at any time in the preceding five years been a director of the company,
-- src:5350 | to give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as may be necessary for the purposes of regulations under this section.
@ref s 412(5) The duty of a director, or a former director of the last five years, to give notice to the company (src:5347-5350)
`s 412(5) the director shall give notice to the company` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `s 412(5) give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as regulations require`
    LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "the director did not give the company notice of the matters regulations require (section 412(5))"

-- the director gives notice: Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 412(5) the director shall give notice to the company` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director DOES `s 412(5) give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as regulations require` AT 7

-- ---- s 414(1): signature ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 414(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 414(1) sign the annual accounts on behalf of the board`

-- src:5387 | (1) A company's annual accounts must be approved by the board of directors and signed on behalf of the board by a director of the company.
@ref s 414(1) Approval by the board and signature by a director (src:5387)
`s 414(1) a director shall sign the annual accounts on behalf of the board` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `s 414(1) sign the annual accounts on behalf of the board`
    LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "no director signed the annual accounts on behalf of the board (section 414(1))"

-- a director signs: Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 414(1) a director shall sign the annual accounts on behalf of the board` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director DOES `s 414(1) sign the annual accounts on behalf of the board` AT 4
